An enum with `option allow_alias = true` must contain at least two values sharing the same number. If all enum values have distinct numbers, the enum is invalid according to the protobuf language specification.

```proto
enum Example {
  option allow_alias = true;

  ZERO = 0;
  ONE = 1;
  TWO = 2;
}
```

This is an error. Remove `allow_alias` when no aliases are needed.
